# Quarry (D735), the small block game: a land of blocks drawn from the
# World's seed, which players dig and build on, the server deciding. Every
# block is an entity of its own, persistent. The game is VoxelTech's class
# among the constitution's reference games at generation 1's scale:
# procedural land, a World players change, and (to come) machines and a
# land kept between runs; chunked storage, meshing, and streaming wait for
# the voxel contract SPEC-0037 and ADR-0058 defer.
program quarry.kest

component 5c3e5cc3-74d0-4669-8cb9-08ee3e1ec13d quarry.terrain Terrain
component 19d85c29-6787-4293-ad64-5078eb4255c7 quarry.block Block
component 0f03f35b-6f21-46f9-8780-a71c82028ccb quarry.digger Digger
component 61646d7c-70f6-4a5d-b965-b39c0c8c1ea4 quarry.tool Tool

# The land is made a few columns a tick from the seed its first tick draws;
# then each player digs or builds where its tool aims.
system quarry.generate simulation generate write quarry.terrain entities random land
system quarry.dig simulation dig read quarry.tool write quarry.digger entities lookup quarry.block lookup quarry.terrain after quarry.generate

spawn 1 quarry.terrain

replicate quarry.block quarry.terrain quarry.digger
player quarry.tool quarry.digger
input quarry.tool
